TITLE:: FxChainPanel
summary:: a chain's effects, stacked, each with its own panel
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/FxChain, Classes/FxChainGUI, Classes/ParaEQPanel, Classes/CompressorPanel

DESCRIPTION::
One strip per effect - its name, and buttons to move or drop it - over the
effect's own panel, which is where all of its controls are. Above them the
chain's row: on/off, its name and bus, the chain presets, and a button per
effect class that is installed. The panel follows the chain: an effect added
from code turns up, one removed goes away.

code::
panel = FxChainPanel(chain);
window.layout = VLayout(panel.view, hints.view);
panel.hints = hints;
panel.running = true;          // the analysers, while it is showing
panel.remove;                  // in window.onClose
::

link::Classes/ServerView:: embeds this under its counters; link::Classes/FxChainGUI::
puts it in a window.

